=== p2-windows · W7 · page:charging/TeslaChargingHistory (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:charging/TeslaChargingHistory   kind=page   web route=/tesla-charging-history
Web source  : web/src/features/charging/pages/TeslaChargingHistoryPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) + maui-windows workload — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  TeslaChargingSessionsPage does. The generated prompt's idealized "TeslaChargingHistoryPage.xaml + ViewModel.cs
  under TeslaSync/Features/Charging" is mapped onto these real conventions. The surface registers itself with the W4
  ShellPageFactory by route name ("TeslaChargingHistory") in ShellWindow.xaml.cs; the nav RouteTable already maps
  Page("TeslaChargingHistory","tesla-charging-history",Charging).
- Data binding (ADR-004): the manifest data sources are bound through the generated OpenAPI contract client
  (TeslaChargingHistoryPage.Source.cs / TeslaChargingHistoryClientFeed) — useTeslaChargingHistory →
  get_api_v1_tesla_charging_history (GET /tesla/charging/history/, snake_case `vin` query, omitted for "All
  Vehicles"); useVehicles → get_api_v1_vehicles (GET /vehicles/); useRefreshTeslaChargingHistory →
  post_api_v1_tesla_charging_history_refresh (POST /tesla/charging/history/refresh, `vin` query). All operation ids
  (incl. the invoice download get_api_v1_tesla_charging_invoice_contentID) are confirmed present in
  apps/windows/Generated/Api/ApiEndpoints.cs. No HTTP touches the view; the ViewModel reads through the injected
  ITeslaChargingHistoryFeed (default EmptyTeslaChargingHistoryFeed = empty state). getTeslaChargingInvoiceURL is a
  direct <a href> URL builder, reproduced as TeslaChargingHistoryRegistration.InvoiceUrl (path /api/v1/tesla/charging/
  invoice/{id}) and pinned per-row in TeslaChargingHistoryRowDisplay.InvoiceUrl.
- Envelope/SI: TeslaChargingHistorySnapshot.FromJson unwraps the platform httputil.Respond {data:{entries,summary}}
  envelope before reading the snake_case entries[]/summary so the wire shape round-trips losslessly. Energy is read
  as SI watt-hours and converted ONLY at the display boundary: the Total-Energy card and the table Energy column both
  via the shared UnitFormatters.FormatEnergy(_wh, units) (web formatEnergy(_, {precision:1})). Spend/avg-cost/cost
  format through ScalarFormatters.FormatCurrency (web formatCurrency / formatCurrencyValue), the rate column through
  NumberFormatting.Format + "/" + (pricing_type ?? "kWh") (web fmtNumber(rate_base,3)), the duration column
  reproduces web durationMinutes + formatDurationMinutes, and the monthly chart reproduces web buildMonthlySpending
  (YYYY-MM bucket, summed total_due, sorted ascending).
- Client-side filters (web parity): the page reproduces the web's two in-memory filters — the location SearchInput
  (TeslaChargingHistoryProjection.FilterBySearch on site_location_name, case-insensitive; web useFilteredList) and the
  RangePicker date filter (FilterByRange on charge_start_datetime; web entries useMemo). Both re-project WITHOUT a
  network round-trip (ViewModel.SetSearch / SetRange). The summary stat cards bind to response.summary and are
  deliberately NOT narrowed by the range filter (web reads summary directly) — pinned by
  Stat_cards_read_the_api_summary_not_the_filtered_rows. The active-filter chip (TsActiveFilterChips) shows only when a
  search query is set, with Remove/Clear wired to ViewModel.ClearSearch.
- States (ADR-006): the web renders its regions inside PageContainer (loading/error). The native port reproduces the
  four data states as visible Fluent regions — loading -> TsStatGridSkeleton(4)+TsTableSkeleton shimmer; error ->
  TsQueryError (InfoBar-equivalent) + Retry (ActionInvoked -> RefreshAsync); success/empty content -> the controls bar
  + four TsStatCards + the monthly-spending TsChartContainer + the session TsDataTable, each region with its own empty
  state (chart noChartData, table noData when no in-range entries, noMatches when the search filters them all out).
  The stat cards/controls render in BOTH success and empty (matching the web, which only swaps the chart/table bodies
  for empty states), so the user can still Refresh.
- i18n (ADR-014): all 31 manifest keys resolve through the ILocalizer facade with the verbatim web key names. 28 were
  already present in Strings/en|ar|he/Resources.resw (translation.tesla_charging.* / translation.charging.invoice /
  translation.table.bulkActions.exportCsv); the 3 the web page uses that the catalog lacked —
  tesla_charging.col.cost_decimal (the catalog carried the older col.cost variant), tesla_charging.monthlySpending.aria
  and tesla_charging.selectVehicle — were added verbatim to all three catalogs in alphabetical position. No literal is
  hardcoded. The invoice column resolves charging.invoice (cell text) + tesla_charging.col.invoice (header) +
  tesla_charging.downloadInvoice (the table's AutomationProperties.HelpText describing the downloadable affordance).
- The invoice cell is text in the shared TsDataTable (which renders text cells); the web <a href> is reproduced as the
  resolved "Invoice" affordance text plus the per-row InvoiceUrl (computed + asserted) and the accessible
  download-invoice help text — a faithful Fluent-native adaptation, never a blank/stub region.
- Microsoft.UI-free Model/Source/ViewModel links were added to TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj (the bare WinUI view is
  excluded — it uses Microsoft.UI). The namespace-local internal JsonReadHelpers + the shared TeslaChargingVehicle /
  TeslaChargingVehicleOption records (sibling TeslaChargingSessionsPage.Model.cs, same Charging namespace) are reused
  (DRY); a record-local null-tolerant bool reader handles has_invoice.
- Build/lint defect found + fixed in this surface's own new code (no red shipped): the Model.cs reference to the
  shared FilterChip needed `using TeslaSync.App.Core.Forms;` — added (the missing using cascaded into the App XAML
  compiler's WMC0001 type-resolution errors until fixed). The five new files were normalised from CRLF to LF to
  satisfy dotnet format ENDOFLINE. All repaired; the app + solution build 0 errors and dotnet format reports 0 changes.

